--- ISSUE 4/7 ---
id: SEM-001
severity: moderate
category: semantics
found_by: static
title: Use exactly one h1 per page
problem: 1 document(s) with more than one <h1> — there should be exactly one top-level heading per page.
why_it_matters: Multiple h1s erode the document outline that screen readers and search engines rely on; a single h1 anchors the page topic.
standards: wcag:1.3.1
locations:
  - docs/cto-eli5-audit-2026-06-10.html:125:7 ~6b74
     122|   <main>
     123|     <div class="hero">
